:"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"050ca64f2fae42859c44f1886a6ec3a201bff9ee8af94bc3f6525c8ca3fc4acb","event_uuid":"9c3629c6-14eb-4154-911f-136d2a864240","position":{"commit_sha":"d61cb9bbd7b9948a210c53fce202bf0c4673fc28","position":"1784761055802029391-9c3629c6-14eb-4154-911f-136d2a864240"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-218_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"c85c122f-abd5-42a2-b149-a7cff1cc6853","comments":[],"created_at":1784760301970512001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## What\n`rebar review-code` assembles its diff with a TWO-dot range `git diff base..head`\n(`src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py`). When `head` is behind `base` (reviewing a PR branch\nnot caught up to `origin/main`), a two-dot diff shows `head` relative to base's CURRENT tip, so\nevery commit merged into `base` since the branch point appears as a spurious deletion. This\ninflates the review with a revert of unrelated work and produces phantom-deletion findings that\ncite real line numbers but describe changes the PR never made. Reported upstream from a client\nproject: a 7-file PR reviewed as 11 files with ~720 phantom deletions; 3 of 5 findings were\nartifacts.\n\n## Approach\nSwitch both diff invocations in `assemble_diff_context` from `base..head` to the THREE-dot\n`base...head` (merge-base) form, matching git's own PR-review convention. Three-dot diffs `head`\nagainst the merge-base of base and head, excluding unrelated commits on `base` after the branch\npoint. The change is limited to the `diff_text is None` git path; the supplied-`diff_text` offline\nseam is unaffected.\n\n## Scope / files\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py` — two `_git` diff calls (`diff` and `diff --name-only`).\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_assemble.py` — new behavioral regression test.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- A branch behind its base reviews ONLY the branch's own changed files; commits merged into base\n  after the branch point are not surfaced as deletions.\n- New regression test `test_diff_is_merge_base_three_dot_not_two_dot` builds a real repo with a\n  branch behind main and asserts `changed_files == [\"feat.py\"]` (no phantom `other.py`); it fails\n  under two-dot and passes under three-dot.\n- lint, typecheck, and the assemble test module stay green.\n\n## Out of scope\nRun-to-run non-determinism and the supply-chain/severity findings from the same upstream report\nare tracked separately.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4aa4dd21-5648-4272-b1a2-e2b484adba91","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8559-44c3-e08a-4bb9","ticket_type":"bug","title":"code-review --base uses two-dot diff; reviewing a branch behind base surfaces phantom deletions","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["56b0506e-4560-40d8-a0fa-aa50ee3138ac","4aa4dd21-5648-4272-b1a2-e2b484adba91","c98021e5-8b20-4bd7-aa9d-cebba67c7e6d","9c3629c6-14eb-4154-911f-136d2a864240"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1784761055802029392,"uuid":"32ce3bd1-f464-4337-911f-6bf680ed19ce"}